  <figure class="about-photo"><img src="/img/willie-jackson.jpg" alt="Portrait of Willie Jackson" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 22rem, 100vw"></figure>
  <div class="about-copy">
    <h1>The hardest problems aren’t structural. They’re human.</h1>
    <p>I started as an IT consultant: enterprise software deployments at Accenture, then years building digital platforms and learning infrastructure. I kept gravitating toward a harder problem. How do you get people to actually change, and how do you build organizations where that change sticks?</p>
    <p>That question led me to Seth Godin’s altMBA, where I was Founding Technical Lead on a leadership program now reaching 7,000+ professionals in 100+ countries. It led me to found Abernathy, a magazine on Black leadership and identity, and then to ReadySet, where I spent six years leading inclusive leadership programs for 200+ organizations, ultimately as Partner and Head of Growth.</p>
    <p>Today I partner with organizations on AI upskilling, leadership development, and large-scale change. No junior team between us, and no off-the-shelf curriculum. Based in Dallas, working with clients globally.</p>
    <p class="aside">Keynotes, writing and events live at <a href="{{ site.author.url }}">williejackson.com</a>. You can also find me on <a href="{{ site.linkedin }}">LinkedIn</a>.</p>
  </div>
</div>

